Log viewer crash FIXED:
  PyQt6: `setLineHeight(height, int)` needs
  `int(QTextBlockFormat.LineHeightTypes.ProportionalHeight.value)`


CODE CHANGES THIS SESSION
-------------------------
core/Utils.py
  - ensureDefaultFontLoaded() registers all four Noto Sans faces
  - activeFontFamily() → Noto Sans (non-retro) or Press Start (retro)
  - FONT_ROLE_SIZES non-retro side set to 10
  - tableDefaultRowHeight / applyTableRowMetrics (platform-aware)
  - nonRetroPlatformStylesheet: Windows table/list item padding → 0
  - applyRoleFonts applies table row metrics to every QTableWidget
core/Query.py buildTable
  - sets default section size BEFORE setRowCount (so rows pick up height)
  - uses Utils.tableDefaultRowHeight (win non-retro tighter)
core/Config.py
  - defaultFontLoaded flag
ui/fonts/
  - NotoSans-*.ttf + LICENSE-NotoSans.txt; Terminess removed
documentation/button-layout-inventory.txt
  - ABS/LAY inventory of all buttons (baseline before Seifer moves)


